## Trap notes

- Stale gateway on 127.0.0.1:7300 breaks consumer-ux tests (EADDRINUSE). Before a suite run: `ss -tln | grep 7300`; stop leftover via `agentide gateway stop` (pattern from post-release-validation).
- The post-release-validation `validate-release.sh` writes the real `~/.config/platform/config.toml`; after a validation run the config may point at a dead gateway — `agentide init --data-dir <scratch>` (or edit) before relying on zero-flag remote in scripts. `config.toml` can now also carry `data_dir = "global" | "repo"`.
- Terminal tool uses `sh` (no bash-isms in one-liners: no `${PIPESTATUS[@]}`, no `[[ ]]`).
- `nv check-banned-types.sh` bans literal `: unknown` in source strings.
- Workspace root ALSO holds a stale `sessions/` copy (`/home/spanexx/Shared/Learn/Agent-Bridge-SDK/sessions/`) alongside the canonical repo-tracked `agentide/sessions/` — legacy double-write; leave both, main.sh may still read the old one.

